          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. 25 vs 35 vs 50 Pint: Which GE Size
          </h2>

          <p>
            The pint figure is how much water the unit is rated to remove in 24 hours under the DOE procedure, which since 2019 has been run at 65 degrees and 60 percent humidity. That is a cool, damp basement condition, so a 50 pint rating is a realistic basement number, and the same machine will pull more on a hot, humid day. Older GE models rated under the previous test carried bigger numbers, such as 70 pints, for similar hardware.
          </p>

