        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Which GE dehumidifier is best?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                For most homes, the 50 pint ADHE50BWF. It has Smart Dry, three fan speeds, a 15 pint bucket and a garden-hose drain, and Total Home Supply lists it as ENERGY STAR certified. Choose the ADHE50PWF if you need a pump, and the ADHE50WWF if you want SmartHQ app control.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does the GE 50 pint dehumidifier have a pump?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Only the ADHE50PWF. GE's dealer store says its built-in pump can drain to a location up to 16 feet away, and the Amazon listing describes 15 feet of vertical lift with a 16 foot hose. The ADHE50BWF and ADHE50WWF drain by bucket or by a garden hose running downhill to a drain.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How big is the GE dehumidifier bucket?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The 50 pint ADHE models have a 15 pint bucket, a little under two gallons, according to Total Home Supply and GE's dealer store. We could not find a published bucket size for the 25 and 35 pint models. At full output a 50 pint unit fills 15 pints quickly, so plan on a hose.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Are GE dehumidifiers discontinued?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The ADHE models are being phased out. GE Appliances' pages mark the ADHE25BWF, ADHE35BWF, ADHE50BWF and ADHE50PWF as no longer manufactured, at clearance prices. ENERGY STAR lists a newer ADSE series certified in November 2025. GE is still in the dehumidifier business; the lineup is changing generations.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is GE Smart Dry?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Smart Dry is GE's automatic fan control. GE's listings describe it as adjusting fan speed based on room humidity, so the unit runs faster when the room is well above your target and slows as it gets close. That reduces noise and energy once a space is near its set point.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What warranty do GE dehumidifiers have?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                GE's dealer store lists the ADHE50PWF with a limited one-year exchange-only parts warranty and no labor, and Total Home Supply describes a one-year replacement for the basic and Wi-Fi 50 pint models. In short, GE replaces a unit that fails in the first year rather than repairing it.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a GE dehumidifier better than a Midea Cube?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not in drying power; current 50 pint models from both brands carry similar ENERGY STAR ratings. GE offers a conventional shape, three fan speeds and Smart Dry. The Midea Cube offers a much larger bucket, up to 4.25 gallons, and nests for storage. If you drain by hose, either works well.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
