        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            GE makes dependable, conventional dehumidifiers, and the ADHE50BWF is the one to buy for a damp basement: 50 pints a day, Smart Dry, three fan speeds and a garden-hose drain. Pay for the ADHE50PWF only if you cannot drain by gravity, and for the ADHE50WWF only if you will use the app. The 35 suits a moderately humid space; the 25 is hard to recommend over it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Go in with open eyes about two things. The ADHE models are the outgoing generation, so check the model number and expect the newer ADSE series to replace them, and the warranty is a one-year exchange. Keep the receipt, clean the filter when the light tells you to, and a GE should serve you well.
